# The external inputs of scripts/bundle-cc.sh (stage 26f): FILE SHA256 URL… (tried in
# order; each download is checked against SHA256). The release job caches the
# downloads keyed by this file's hash, and on master copies them to the release
# `bundle-inputs` of this repository, which is the last mirror tried.
# A $U in a URL is an Ubuntu pool (pool/main/...), $R the bundle-inputs release.
#
# The sysroot inputs (libc6, libc6-dev, linux-libc-dev) are glibc 2.27 and Linux 4.15
# headers from Ubuntu 18.04, which is EOL (2023-05). They are link-time only:
# share/wiz/cc is `clang --sysroot=...`, and the programs it builds link the host's
# glibc dynamically, so no 18.04 code runs in a release. 2.27 is a compatibility
# *floor* for those programs, chosen so they run on the oldest distribution anyone
# might still use. Ubuntu 18.04 is the last distribution that requires 2.27; everything
# supported in 2026 needs 2.28 or later (RHEL 8, the oldest still-supported one, has
# 2.28 and is supported to 2029-05; Debian 10, 2.28, went EOL in 2024-06). Moving the
# floor to 2.28 would drop 18.04 and is a support-policy decision, not a build detail.
# TODO(2026-11-17, wiz-pl maintainers): decide whether to move the sysroot to a
# supported release (glibc 2.28 or later) and drop the Ubuntu 18.04 floor; until then
# this pin is deliberate and link-only, not a stale comment.
